# OpenVPN, statically linked, with mbedTLS rather than OpenSSL.
#
# mbedTLS because it is the right trade here, not merely a smaller one: it
# cross-builds in about a minute against OpenSSL's ten, which across this
# matrix is the difference between ten minutes a release and eighty. The
# binary is smaller with it too.
#
# What mbedTLS costs, from upstream's own README.mbedtls:
#
#   * no PKCS#12. A provider handing out a .p12 has to be unpacked into
#     separate ca/cert/key first -- one openssl pkcs12 command, on a PC.
#   * no --capath. --ca with a single file works; a directory of CAs does not.
#   * X.509 alternative username fields must be CN.
#   * the subject line handed to scripts and plugins is formatted differently
#     than OpenSSL's, which matters only if something parses it.
#
# Inline <ca>, <cert>, <key> and <tls-crypt> blocks -- what almost every .ovpn
# actually contains -- are unaffected.
#
# ONE BINARY, CLIENT AND SERVER. Not a choice made here: --disable-server was
# removed from configure in OpenVPN 2.5 ("it is no longer possible to build a
# client-/p2p-only OpenVPN binary -- the saving in code size no longer
# outweighs the extra maintenance effort"), and --disable-client never existed.
# Which role this runs in is decided by the config file, not by the build.
PKG=openvpn
VERSION=2.7.7
REVISION=1
# The release tarball from the project, not GitHub's archive: the latter has
# no generated configure, and building it would need the full autotools chain
# on every runner.
SOURCE=https://swupdate.openvpn.net/community/releases/openvpn-2.7.7.tar.gz
SHA256=3ab8f48fd6c26d49ba2333a092433949afdb5c85c0e6a1ff265784fbc04a2463
TOOLCHAIN=zig
TARGETS=all

# 3.6.x is the LTS line, and 3.6.4 is the floor for TLS 1.3 support in
# OpenVPN's mbedTLS backend -- below it the tunnel still works, at TLS 1.2.
# Not 4.x: OpenVPN's support for it is new and its own changelog still talks
# about translating algorithm identifiers.
DEPS='mbedtls libcapng'
DEP_SOURCE_mbedtls=https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/releases/download/mbedtls-3.6.7/mbedtls-3.6.7.tar.bz2
DEP_SHA256_mbedtls=a7e8bcbec0e6f761b4af24f25677626b35f762f68eef79c08677a363212d11f6

# libcap-ng is not optional and not avoidable: on Linux OpenVPN 2.7 hard-fails
# configure without it, with no --disable to offer. It is what drops privileges
# when a config says --user/--group.
#
# This is the one recipe here that needs autotools on the build host. Upstream
# stopped publishing dist tarballs after 0.8.5 (2021) and now ships only git
# tags, which carry no generated configure. 0.8.5 was the alternative and was
# rejected: every release since fixes capng_change_id, which is precisely the
# function OpenVPN calls -- supplementary groups in 0.9.6, thread safety in
# 0.9.6, setpcap handling in 0.9.3.
DEP_SOURCE_libcapng=https://github.com/stevegrubb/libcap-ng/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.6.tar.gz
DEP_SHA256_libcapng=399040138e0ca62fa2bcabd63da9af4431a246ef7a654561a0ca3cb00010a539

SMOKE='--version'
SMOKE_EXPECT='OpenVPN 2.7.7'

# UNVERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE: /dev/net/tun. Without the tun driver in the
# box's kernel openvpn cannot create an interface, and no binary can supply
# one. The same caveat packages/wireguard-go carries, for the same reason.
